<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">
<!--
DESIGN LEDGER: handy101 lift subsystem, robot frame imported from base101.
Units m/kg/s/rad. All meshes mm, scale 0.001; link frames +X/+Y/+Z parallel
with CAD and chassis axes. Source: base101_lift.step, source SHA and exact
measurements in config/cad_measurements.json. No original CAD file is modified.

Frame alignment: CAD deck centre (-0.433132508, 1.5) mm and top Z=64.795890279
mm map to base101 deck centre (0,0) and top Z=0.084965 m. Translation only.
The existing ground-centred base_link stays unchanged. Overlay mounts to it.

Links:
 lift_left_structure, lift_right_structure: fixed rigid column assemblies,
 each origin at deck centre/top, same axes as base_link; meshes re-framed there.
 Each contains extrusion, rail, screw, bearing, servo, adapters, end cap/base.
 The screw is visually fixed: prismatic lift motion abstracts the screw drive.
 lift_left_main, lift_right_main: moving assembly; frame at CAD nut bbox centre,
 includes main platform, nut, MGN12 block rigidly together in link-local visuals.
 The obsolete lift_left_carriage and lift_right_carriage are excluded.
 lift_crossbar: aluminum fixed crossbar, frame at deck centre/top.
 head_camera_mount: printed top mount and servo body, fixed to crossbar;
 frame coincident with the crossbar/deck frame, local mm meshes.
 head_camera_link: RealSense body and printed support, framed at the CAD camera
 bbox centre, axes parallel to chassis; exact exported pose is preserved.
 head_camera_mount_joint is fixed identity. head_camera_tilt_joint rotates
 head_camera_tilt_frame about +Y at the measured servo shaft/bearing axis:
 CAD X=10.166866915 mm, Z=681.845890773 mm, Y=3.501471516 mm
 (servo body lateral centre; any point on this axis is equivalent).
 Servo coaxial cylindrical surfaces and both support bearing seats agree.
 head_camera_pose_joint fixes the camera bbox-centred link to this pivot frame.
 q=0 preserves the exported pose; positive +Y tilts the forward camera downward.
 See config/head_tilt_measurements.json. Frame-only pivot adds no physical mass.
 Arms attach to the respective main links through arms.xacro; measured servo
 and shoulder datums establish their transforms independently of these COMs.

Joints:
 left_structure_mount/right_structure_mount: parent -> structure, fixed,
 XYZ (0,0,0.084965), RPY identity, deck alignment above.
 left_lift_joint/right_lift_joint: respective structure -> main, prismatic,
 +Z raises platform; q=0 is the STEP pose and user-confirmed lowest mechanical position.
 Origins copied from CAD nut centres relative to deck, RPY identity.
 crossbar_mount: parent -> crossbar, fixed (0,0,0.084965), RPY identity.

Geometry and inertia:
 Each physical link has link-local material-group STL visuals, identity origins,
 scale 0.001. Extrusions/crossbar/camera housing aluminum, main/top/base/printed
 mounts black plastic, rails/screws/bearings steel, nuts brass.
 Collision: component boxes for columns, combined box for main and crossbar.
 CAD mass/COM/inertia calculations are documented in lift_geometry.xacro and
 config/cad_measurements.json; material densities are assumptions, motors 55 g.
 Shapes are rigid groups; inertials summed with the parallel-axis theorem.

LIMITS AND ASSUMPTIONS:
 Travel [0,0.45] m: 450 mm usable travel confirmed by the user.
 Zero is the STEP pose, confirmed by the user as the lowest possible position.
 Homing sensor and hardware zero calibration are outside this description stage.
 Max force 100 N; max speed 0.02 m/s; viscous damping 30 N s/m; not calibrated.
 Independent lift axes; no mimic constraint or assumed mechanical coupling.
 Screw lead and rotational actuator model not yet known or represented.
 Head tilt range defaults to provisional +/-90 degrees; effort 2 N m, speed
 1 rad/s and damping 0.1 are simulation estimates, not calibrated hardware. The dual mod101 arms are imported separately by arms.xacro. Head motor mass 55 g and camera 72 g are estimates.
 MuJoCo/ROS actuator integration is not implemented by this geometry macro.
-->
  <xacro:arg name="head_tilt_lower" default="-1.5707963267948966"/>
  <xacro:arg name="head_tilt_upper" default="1.5707963267948966"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find handy101_description)/urdf/lift_geometry.xacro"/>
  <xacro:macro name="handy101_lifts" params="parent left_travel:=0.45 right_travel:=0.45">
    <material name="handy_aluminum"><color rgba="0.77 0.78 0.79 1"/></material>
    <material name="handy_black_plastic"><color rgba="0.075 0.075 0.080 1"/></material>
    <material name="handy_steel"><color rgba="0.60 0.605 0.62 1"/></material>
    <material name="handy_brass"><color rgba="0.65 0.48 0.20 1"/></material>
    <xacro:lift_left_structure_geometry/>
    <xacro:lift_right_structure_geometry/>
    <xacro:lift_left_main_geometry/>
    <xacro:lift_right_main_geometry/>
    <xacro:lift_crossbar_geometry/>
    <xacro:head_camera_mount_geometry/>
    <xacro:head_camera_link_geometry/>
    <joint name="left_structure_mount" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${parent}"/><child link="lift_left_structure"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0.084965" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="right_structure_mount" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${parent}"/><child link="lift_right_structure"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0.084965" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="left_lift_joint" type="prismatic">
      <parent link="lift_left_structure"/><child link="lift_left_main"/>
      <origin xyz="-0.000400000627411 0.100001465631 0.0957499878743" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <axis xyz="0 0 1"/>
      <limit lower="0" upper="${left_travel}" effort="100" velocity="0.02"/>
      <dynamics damping="30" friction="0"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="right_lift_joint" type="prismatic">
      <parent link="lift_right_structure"/><child link="lift_right_main"/>
      <origin xyz="-5.75775811862e-10 -0.0999987298309 0.0955499878744" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <axis xyz="0 0 1"/>
      <limit lower="0" upper="${right_travel}" effort="100" velocity="0.02"/>
      <dynamics damping="30" friction="0"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="crossbar_mount" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${parent}"/><child link="lift_crossbar"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0.084965" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="head_camera_mount_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent link="lift_crossbar"/><child link="head_camera_mount"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <link name="head_camera_tilt_frame"/>
    <joint name="head_camera_tilt_joint" type="revolute">
      <parent link="head_camera_mount"/><child link="head_camera_tilt_frame"/>
      <origin xyz="0.0105999994233 0.00200147151639 0.6170500004945" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <axis xyz="0 1 0"/>
      <limit lower="$(arg head_tilt_lower)" upper="$(arg head_tilt_upper)" effort="2" velocity="1"/>
      <dynamics damping="0.1" friction="0"/>
    </joint>
    <!-- Fixed mesh frame offset preserves every visual/inertial at q=0. -->
    <joint name="head_camera_pose_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent link="head_camera_tilt_frame"/><child link="head_camera_link"/>
      <origin xyz="0.0243032963678 0.00004257521064 0.0266071180705" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <!-- Mechanical front-face centre from the STEP camera bounds; exact lens
         principal point remains a calibration datum. Optical Z forward/X right/Y down. -->
    <link name="head_camera_optical_frame"/>
    <joint name="head_camera_optical_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent link="head_camera_link"/><child link="head_camera_optical_frame"/>
      <origin xyz="0.012597239323706 0 0" rpy="-1.5707963267948966 0 -1.5707963267948966"/>
    </joint>
  </xacro:macro>
</robot>
